lens:
CRO (Baymard/CXL school, D2C jewellery India), round 5. Measures add-to-cart and checkout rate for a shopper landing from an Instagram ad at 360x640 in the in-app browser: first-screen decision content, the buy path (Add to bag, Buy now, sticky bar, the moment after adding), the 20% add-to-checkout drop, the Buy 2/3/4 ladder and AOV, COD vs prepaid, ad message match, friction and distraction, and the test plan.

G3 passes. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_1-4.jpg and measure.json (05:41:52-56) are newer than prototype.html (05:41:50), and my renders of an untouched copy (md5 a4a874df...) match them: facts end at 562, the bar starts at 575, the card spans 85-360. fold-ad.png is byte-identical to fold.png (md5 d4ae18d6...), by design.

Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/cro_r5/:
- probe.js and probe.json: the buy path, double taps, the bags with 1-4 pieces, Buy now, folds at five sizes, landings;
- probe2.js and probe2_360x640.json: the card for an add at every scroll position (10px steps to 400, then 50px);
- probe3.json: the card at scrollY 0/40/100 on nine viewports;
- probe4.json: the one-piece bag on short screens, and what the bag's policy line does;
- mock1.js and mock1.json: the 'slim' card;
- mkvar.py, which builds var/prototype.html (fixes 2-4); var_probe2_360x640.json and probe5.json check it;
- screenshots: bag1-4.png, add_at_360_*.png, add0_320x568.png, after_policy_tap.png, mock_slim_*.png, var_bag1.png, var_bag_policy_open.png, var_add_at_360_*.png.
The prototype was not edited.

All four R4 fixes landed. The compact card keeps 'Adjustable, US 5-9' at scrollY 20-80. The bag's top line names the next rung in rupees: '20% off all three with the necklace, ₹460 more', then '30% off all four with the hoops, ₹469 more'. nf_contact, nf_view, nf_fold and nf_size fire. An add at 260-400 now gets a dock.

Two R4 changes cost the buy path something:
(1) The general 'no control under the dock' rule also treats the 396px macro photo and Riya's tiles as controls. Scroll positions where an add gets no card went from 25/60 in R4 to 40/60.
(2) The new policy line in the bag is a link that closes the bag, logs a bag exit and drops her about 2,950px down the page. It also names the refusal but not the remedy.
One older gap also remains: the 'nosug' card at scrollY 90-150 (and at scrollY 0 on 320x568) drops the one-tap ring and the ladder line.
And the test cannot yet be read on orders: nothing puts the arm on a Shopify order.

score_now is the weighted mean of the same 14 criteria as R3 and R4: 674.1 / 76 = 8.87, reported as 8.9. The critique is also saved to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/pdp10/rounds/r5_cro.json.

criteria.note:
R4 fix 4 landed. Every bag line now speaks rupees:
- bag2: '20% off all three with the necklace, ₹460 more';
- bag3: '30% off all four with the hoops, ₹469 more';
